    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Demand loan activity</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Demand loan activity</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ASC 740 considers the equity component of AFUDC a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes must be provided. The Respondent is required to record the deferred tax liability for AFUDC equity in Account 282 with a corresponding regulatory asset. The regulatory asset is itself a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes are recognized and recorded in Account 283. This accounting is also outlined in FERC Docket AI93-5-000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents the probable future recovery of regulatory costs associated with the filing of a general rate case.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Emission Credit CIP Deferral Account is a regulatory asset to record and seek recovery of CIP-related costs that the Company pays during the settlement term plus interest calculated pursuant to the applicable FERC interest rates in its next Section 4 rate proceeding, with costs amortized over a period of no less than seven years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Emission Credit CIP is a regulatory asset established pursuant to the previous rate case settlement, with costs amortized over three years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate Schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The volumes used to calculate the Annual Charge Assessment are 1,165,872,461 Dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Gas Transmission Northwest &#8220;Fuel and Line Loss Percentage&#8221; does not identify separate fuel and loss components.&#160; Therefore, all gas retained from shippers is reported as &#8220;Gas Received from Shippers as Compressor Station Fuel&#8221;.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Receipts represent the decreases in linepack.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate Schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Deliveries and Gas Used for Other Operations represent the increases in linepack and Gas Used for Other Operations.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Lines 9 through 29 are allocated to each rate type: Discounted Rate, Negotiated Rate and Recourse Rate, using a pro-rata allocation.&#160; The pro-rata share is determined by dividing the Shipper Supplied Gas for each rate type by the total Shipper Supplied gas for lines 2 through 6 and multiplying by the corresponding monthly totals for lines 9 through 29.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">WACOG of $2.73 is used for pricing of gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent has a Commission Approved Adjustment Mechanism For Fuel, Loss and Other Unaccounted for Gas that tracks shipper supplied gas.&#160; The applicable excess or deficient balance is included in the next monthly retention calculation to collect deficiencies or pass back excesses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate Schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate Schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The incremental project has a 0% fuel rate.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The incremental project has a 0% fuel rate.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The incremental project has a 0% fuel rate.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Rate of Return utilized is an actual three year average rate.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Inventory method is used.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Refer to Note 2(k) - Income Taxes and Note 4 - Income Taxes in the Notes to the Financial Statements on Page 122.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Refer to Note 2(k) - Income Taxes and Note 4 - Income Taxes in the Notes to the Financial Statements on Page 122.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Refer to Note 2(k) - Income Taxes and Note 4 - Income Taxes in the Notes to the Financial Statements on Page 122.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Refer to Note 2(k) - Income Taxes and Note 4 - Income Taxes in the Notes to the Financial Statements on Page 122.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Refer to Note 2(k) - Income Taxes and Note 4 - Income Taxes in the Notes to the Financial Statements on Page 122.</link:footnote>
